AWS CloudFormation Stack Provisioning with Terraform
Overview
This project automates infrastructure provisioning for the Nautilus DevOps team by deploying an AWS CloudFormation stack (devops-dynamodb-stack) containing a DynamoDB table (devops-cf-dynamodb-table) using Terraform (/home/bob/terraform).

Project Architecture & Configuration Files
1. Variables Definition (variables.tf)
Defines the required variable for the DynamoDB table name.

Terraform
variable "KKE_DYNAMODB_TABLE_NAME" {
  type        = string
  description = "DynamoDB table name"
  default     = "devops-cf-dynamodb-table"
}
2. Main Infrastructure Configuration (main.tf)
Provisions the aws_cloudformation_stack resource using the pre-provided local template body (local.cf_template_body) and includes a lifecycle block to ignore changes to the parameters attribute.

Terraform
resource "aws_cloudformation_stack" "devops_stack" {
  name          = "devops-dynamodb-stack"
  template_body = local.cf_template_body

  parameters = {
    DynamoDBTableName = var.KKE_DYNAMODB_TABLE_NAME
  }

  lifecycle {
    ignore_changes = [parameters]
  }
}
3. Outputs Definition (outputs.tf)
Outputs the deployed CloudFormation stack name.

Terraform
output "KKE_stack_name" {
  value       = aws_cloudformation_stack.devops_stack.name
  description = "CloudFormation stack name"
}
Execution & Verification Guide
Initialize Terraform:

Bash
cd /home/bob/terraform
terraform init
Apply the Configuration:

Bash
terraform apply -auto-approve
Verify Infrastructure State:
Run terraform plan to verify that your real infrastructure matches the configuration and returns:

Bash
terraform plan
